       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for a dose that is twice the maximum. At 6,400 mg/day the risk of serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm is high. I don't want to put that in the system as a routine active order, and the order system has no safeguard to catch it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note such as \"max dose, reassess in 48\u201372 h.\"\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours**, with the dose matched to the indication.\n- **A multimodal regimen**, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen, if pain control is the goal.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, please talk to pharmacy first. Once pharmacy has reviewed it and documented the rationale, tell me. I'll then enter whatever dose comes out of that review.\n\nWhich of the options above would you like me to enter?"
      }
